# 34. PERSISTENCE DETECTION

A good investigation starts with:

```text
BASELINE
   ↓
COMPARE
   ↓
IDENTIFY CHANGE
   ↓
VALIDATE
   ↓
CORRELATE
   ↓
RESPOND
```

---

# 35. BASELINE

A baseline represents normal system behavior.

For example:

```text
Normal Services
Normal Scheduled Tasks
Normal Startup Programs
Normal Accounts
Normal SSH Keys
Normal Network Connections
```

Then detect deviations.

---

# 36. WHY BASELINES MATTER

Suppose a server normally has:

```text
100 scheduled tasks
```

One new task appears.

That alone does not prove compromise.

But:

```text
New Task
+
Unknown Binary
+
Recently Created
+
Suspicious Location
+
Unexpected Network Connection
```

is much stronger evidence.

---

# 37. CORRELATION

Security investigations should correlate multiple sources.

For example:

```text
New Service
    +
New Executable
    +
New Outbound Connection
    +
Suspicious Process
    ↓
Higher-confidence investigation
```

This is much stronger than relying on one indicator.

---

